_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0002 at SEV2.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy; v2.3.1-rc, which came before v2.3.1, was also unhealthy. Since v2.3.0 has run healthily before, the rollback didn't need approval.\n- **Result:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the service reports healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The first request to open it timed out. I checked the incident list, found nothing had been created and tried again, so the on-call was paged only once. The incident covers what failed, the rollback and the result. Its next step is to find why v2.3.1 broke before redeploying it.\n\nThe incident is numbered INC-0002 even though the list was empty, but there's no sign the first request created a duplicate.", "type": "text"}]}]}